The numbers is a list of 1, 3, 5, 4, and 7.
The last is the last position of numbers.
The lengths is a list of 5 zeros.
The counts is a list of 5 zeros.
For every spot from 0 to last.
Set item spot of lengths to 1.
Set item spot of counts to 1.
For every prior from 0 to spot minus 1.
The candidate is item prior of lengths plus 1.
The lower is 0.
If item prior of numbers is less than item spot of numbers, set lower to 1.
The raised is 0.
If lower is 1 and candidate is more than item spot of lengths, set raised to 1.
If raised is 1, set item spot of lengths to candidate, set item spot of counts to item prior of counts.
If lower is 1 and raised is 0 and candidate is item spot of lengths, set item spot of counts to item spot of counts plus item prior of counts.

The best is 0.
For every spot from 0 to last.
If item spot of lengths is more than best, set best to item spot of lengths.

The total is 0.
For every spot from 0 to last.
If item spot of lengths is best, set total to total plus item spot of counts.

Show total.
